{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting","id":850434,"title":"A Mage Toronto Setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-20T23:20:38-07:00","id":850434,"title":"A Mage Toronto Setting","content":"So, exciting news. My girlfriend and I are contemplating trying to do more connective tissue between our games, and her upcoming Werewolf game set in Toronto is setting up to be the basis for that.<br /> <br /> So, my aspiration for this is to set up a Consilium for Toronto in anticipation of running a game of Mage set there, and while I'm absolutely nerve-wracked thinking about how to set up the Consilium (I'm want to use it to introduce the idea of Mage society to the players, but I also want it to be interesting.) and one of the biggest questions is what to make the Mystery for the setting.<br /> <br /> Now, I'll admit, this is a part where I'm horrible. I've read that Toronto can uncharitably be described as &quot;New York without the famous landmarks&quot; and I've also heard it's one of the most diverse cities in the world. I'm wondering what kind of history the city has that might lend itself to Mages investigating a mystery there. Does anyone know more about the city and care to chime in, maybe offer some suggestions?<br /> <br /> I'm looking at the Chicago book for ideas on how to structure the cross-splat relationships, but each game is going to be standalone in the sense that players will be playing Mages or Werewolves but not really both.<br /> <br /> Relatedly, does anyone have any ideas for a good intersection between a conventional consilium set up and an interesting idea? ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> I will love you forever if you throw me a bone on this one)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T00:23:19-07:00","id":850445,"title":"","content":"I lived in the city for a span of almost two decades and, to be honest, &quot;New York without the famous landmarks&quot; is probably a fair assessment. Our most famous landmark is an enormous radio mast. Somehow, we managed to elect a crack-addicted man-potato as mayor who haunted the background of every photo he was in. There is a surprisingly public mafia presence but very little talk of it since it's violent only once in a blue moon.<br /> <br /> It's a city to love and hate with equal measure.<br /> <br /> Some landmarks you'll probably want to look into, as a general rule, are the CN Tower, the Harbourfront (and the Thousand Islands), and Kensington Market. Toronto's also got enough university students between its campuses whose combined populations outrank many US cities. York University has, as of 2015, about 55,000 students alone; U of T has about 84,500 spread between its downtown and satellite campuses.<br /> <br /> The subway system is outstanding, as is public transit in general, and perhaps one of the few things I truly miss about the city. You can get anywhere - <i>anywhere</i> - within the entire city using it.<br /> <br /> As far as the city's history goes, there's definitely information to be found on it, but Toronto's never truly been the epicenter of grand events upon which hinge the fate of nations. Not so far as I know, at least. Anyone can correct me if they wish.<br /> <br /> Its reputation for diversity is well-deserved, though. One of the first news stories I covered there was the closing of The Real Jerk, which was one of the major landmarks in Toronto's Caribbean community, and Chinatown almost feels like another country. It's also got some striking economic diversity, since it is a city with property values to rival New York in parts, and one which still hosts many soup kitchens and charities to help feed its people, and it gets especially striking when these areas are almost side by side. High Park is a particularly striking example.<br /> <br /> I'll ruminate on Mystery suggestions. The Thousand Islands might be a good place to start; there's tons of myths associated with them, including claims of them spontaneously rearranging or appearing and disappearing. You might also consider the persistence of diversity in the city. Perhaps the Thousand Islands are a very large, very weak Astral Verge; each island a home for one of the city's many cultures. Under the right circumstances, the verge thins considerably, and things start walking through, and crossing into the city atop night fog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T01:39:58-07:00","id":850453,"title":"","content":"For 2ED setting building, it sounds most important as to determine local High Weirdness/Main Mystery of region. I never been in Canada, but your's description sounds as Toronto is very &quot;boring&quot; place. Maybe it is TOO boring? How about this idea...<br /> <br /> <i>Toronto is quite place. Too quite for the metropolis like this. Awakened of the area point that Lie is especially strong in city. There are very low numbers of sorcerers to the comparable place on planet or to the other supernaturals populations in the city itself. Awakenings are rare. Both Seers and Pentacle points there is some... force - that stops many started Mystery Plays. Exarchs Servants takes it as blessing from their Supernal Masters. Diamond try's to understand this Mystery and found <b>other</b> explanation to this, to weak local Tetrarchy sway - but Ministries evidances are strong ones for many. Only Free Council do not fight it - in reality, Assembly fights for survival, after last wars with oppressing forces working for the Throne and Lie. Welcome to Toronto, Canada's most quite place.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T01:49:18-07:00","id":850454,"title":"","content":"I think in Left Hand Path it mentions that Toronto is politically dominated by the Tremere. They don't act openly, but every Heirarch has gotten their position by surrendering their soul to the Tremere who keep it in an artifact the Chalice of Souls. The artifact maintains your metaphysical connection to your soul so you aren't affected by its absence, but it gives the Tremere insurance that they can devour it if you cross them. In return they take the heirarch's side in matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T07:50:12-07:00","id":850550,"title":"","content":"I've said this before, I think, but the web novel Pact is a great example of a Mage chronicle set in Toronto. It even includes Changeling sideplot, Abyssal invaders, an Archmaster or two, Spirits, Ghosts, and a few things that could be called Beasts now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://pactwebserial.wordpress.com/table-of-contents/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://s0.wp.com/i/blank.jpg?m=1383295312i\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pactwebserial.wordpress.com/table-of-contents/\" target=\"_blank\"> Table of Contents </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pactwebserial.wordpress.com/table-of-contents/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://pactwebserial.wordpress.com/table-of-contents/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Arc 1: Bonds 1.01 1.02 1.03 1.04 1.05 1.06 1.07 1.0x&nbsp; (Pages: RDT&rsquo;s Diary #1) Arc 2: Damages 2.01 2.02 2.03 2.04 2.05 2.06 2.0x (Pages: Famulus, Implementum, Demesnes) 2.07 2.0y (Histories: M&hellip; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:37:48-07:00","id":850577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=850454#post850454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in Left Hand Path it mentions that Toronto is politically dominated by the Tremere. They don't act openly, but every Heirarch has gotten their position by surrendering their soul to the Tremere who keep it in an artifact the Chalice of Souls. The artifact maintains your metaphysical connection to your soul so you aren't affected by its absence, but it gives the Tremere insurance that they can devour it if you cross them. In return they take the heirarch's side in matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Chalice Compact, yeah.<br /> <br /> Gotta admit, it's kind of an unflattering picture of the city.<br /> <br /> Still, Toronto's got a huge population; beaten in North America only by New York, Mexico City, Los Angeles, and (just barely) Chicago. If you wanted to be a soul-eating predator, that's almost certainly the place to do it. The Chalice Compact feels like a fatally stupid decision on the part of any Mage who took it, but I can easily imagine wolves hiding among the sheep. Anywhere desperate people flock for a better life, there will be those looking to take advantage of it.<br /> <br /> If the city's Mages know about it, the Sentinel probably watches the mental health services like a hawk. Toronto does have a reasonable amount of those and its crime rate is relatively low, so, unless the Tremere went to extraordinary levels when they snatched a soul, people are gonna find out.<br /> <br /> Still, if there <i>are</i> Tremere in Toronto, they're there for a reason. One reason might simply be that it's utterly unremarkable; a large city without any major Mysteries, making it easy preying grounds since there's so few other Awakened, but that makes for a relatively dull chronicle. At least unless you want to make it &quot;Kill the leeches&quot;.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is that there might be one of the Bound beneath the lake, attracting a large Seer presence to the area; the islands its calcified skin. The Awakened in Toronto may experience strange dreams, and see High Speech patterns written across the surfaces of buildings; endure hallucinations where they see the CN Tower as an Etemenanki and the city as a new Babylon. The Bound <i>wants</i> something, it is trying to <i>do</i> something, and that &quot;something&quot; manifests occasionally as strange alterations of the city. Cults spontaneously appear worshiping &quot;She Who Is The Foundation&quot;; streets and avenues open down secluded alleys that just weren't there before, and those who follow them can disappear into this Second City (see the Crossways in Intruders for inspiration), where the world grows increasingly strange, and starts to resemble tales of the Time Not.<br /> <br /> Toronto is meant to be more than what it is; something to rival any of the world's grandest cities. And yet it isn't. <i>Someone</i> is keeping it that way.<br /> <br /> And maybe that's for the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:36:58-07:00","id":850621,"title":"","content":"I think that the influence the Chalice Compact has in the book sounds less interesting, but I do like the idea that the Tremere are an issue there and that they may support certain mages in the Consilium in exchange for their protection.<br /> <br /> I'll look into <i>Intruders </i>for the inspiration, though that also sounds like the Prince of 10,000 Leaves, which could be cool as a possible enemy.<br /> <br /> The thought occurs to me that with such a large immigration population coming into Toronto that it could have a small apostate community that exists alongside the Consilium. Would it be bad to have an antagonistic relationship between them and the Pentacle, which might perceive them as untrustworthy? Or would that make them look too hawkish?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:50:35-07:00","id":850632,"title":"","content":"The Prince of Ten-Thousand Leaves is a neat antagonist, but making a Supernal equivalent to the Crossways - an Emanation Realm, of sorts - strikes me as more fun just because it'd make player characters less likely to want to tear it down straight away. In my experience, players either treat the Abyss like toxic waste or a swimming pool, rarely in-between (a swimming pool of toxic waste?). Once it's Supernal, it becomes something that makes them curious, even if it's dangerous, because, hey, Supernal means good by default, right?<br /> <br /> Right?<br /> <br /> As far as a large apostate community... Yeah, I can totally see that. Great idea. I wouldn't make them antagonistic, though. If you want to capture the spirit of Toronto, make them... Separate. The migrant Awakened coming to Toronto who aren't able to blend in with Western culture would suffer the same problem most new migrants have. Even if they're already a member of an Atlantean Order - which many may be - they're still facing entirely different traditions and expectations. A gloss of familiarity isn't the same thing as being the same.<br /> <br /> Toronto, like a lot of Canada, has a big civic mandate of embracing diversity, rather than a melting pot, and, while that produces some awesome things, it has this habit of causing Toronto to feel like a patchwork quilt rather than a unified whole. People separate themselves into little bubbles, and many first generation migrants simply don't leave their community unless they have to or unless they have their second generation children to translate for them. It's particularly common in Toronto's Chinese community, as far as I've seen.<br /> <br /> The Consilium of Toronto might not be far off. Sure, they communicate with the apostate community/communities, but there's probably a definitive Us and Them feel going on. Not Us <i>versus</i> Them, but definitely an unspoken barrier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T12:30:53-07:00","id":850740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=850453#post850453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For 2ED setting building, it sounds most important as to determine local High Weirdness/Main Mystery of region. I never been in Canada, but your's description sounds as Toronto is very &quot;boring&quot; place. Maybe it is TOO boring? How about this idea...<br /> <br /> <i>Toronto is quite place. Too quite for the metropolis like this. Awakened of the area point that Lie is especially strong in city. There are very low numbers of sorcerers to the comparable place on planet or to the other supernaturals populations in the city itself. Awakenings are rare. Both Seers and Pentacle points there is some... force - that stops many started Mystery Plays. Exarchs Servants takes it as blessing from their Supernal Masters. Diamond try's to understand this Mystery and found <b>other</b> explanation to this, to weak local Tetrarchy sway - but Ministries evidances are strong ones for many. Only Free Council do not fight it - in reality, Assembly fights for survival, after last wars with oppressing forces working for the Throne and Lie. Welcome to Toronto, Canada's most quite place.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not having a go at you Wyrd, but I'd say no way to this description. As an Albertan, I've taken more than a a few cracks at Toronto over the years, but that's more of a rivalry based on loyalty to cities that consider themselves (usually friendly) rivals. <br /> <br /> Toronto is diverse. Toronto is large. Toronto is insanely devoted to a hockey team I'll never understand (though they'd likely say the same thing about the Flames). Toronto had a mayor who was briefly the target of comedians worldwide. <br /> <br /> The one thing Toronto has never, ever been is boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T14:27:40-07:00","id":850804,"title":"","content":"Another possibility would be to break up the Pentacle. I mean, the Orders exist in other forms all across the world. It'd be quite possible that there are outposts of other caucuses who are not terribly happy about the idea of just being subsummed into what passes for traditional Pentacle society in Toronto.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T10:30:40-07:00","id":851217,"title":"","content":"Two things: <br /> <br /> 1) I stumbled upon this article today and thought it may be useful: <a href=\"http://news.nationalpost.com/life/travel/top-five-must-sees-in-toronto-from-the-wonderfully-terrifying-edge-walk-to-multicultural-delights?__lsa=9e0a-1104\" target=\"_blank\">http://news.nationalpost.com/life/tr..._lsa=9e0a-1104</a><br /> <br /> 2) On a much more somber note that those of you outside of Canada may not have heard, Rob Ford, the infamous former mayor of the city, passed away from cancer today. While it shouldn't change anything your do or say, you may want to be mindful of that moving on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:18:16-07:00","id":851388,"title":"","content":"You might what to look at the Changeling 2e spoiler for the Toronto Courts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HTskUNzJBu6g-_LP_HDyVfQUHE-x4MCinb3GyWZxhp8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HTskUNzJBu6g-_LP_HDyVfQUHE-x4MCinb3GyWZxhp8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HTskUNzJBu6g-_LP_HDyVfQUHE-x4MCinb3GyWZxhp8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HTskUNzJBu6g-_LP_HDyVfQUHE-x4MCinb3GyWZxhp8/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I was toying with using the Toronto Changeling 2e as a starting point for a multi splat write up once the Changeling core came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:27:45-07:00","id":851392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=851388#post851388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might what to look at the Changeling 2e spoiler for the Toronto Courts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HTskUNzJBu6g-_LP_HDyVfQUHE-x4MCinb3GyWZxhp8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HTskUNzJBu6g-_LP_HDyVfQUHE-x4MCinb3GyWZxhp8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HTskUNzJBu6g-_LP_HDyVfQUHE-x4MCinb3GyWZxhp8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HTskUNzJBu6g-_LP_HDyVfQUHE-x4MCinb3GyWZxhp8/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I was toying with using the Toronto Changeling 2e as a starting point for a multi splat write up once the Changeling core came out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I already incorporated the Cult of Mitra in my write up, that's a great weird organization to have in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T17:57:18-07:00","id":851479,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd add in that I can see Mages being all over the Kensington Market's Goblin Market. Huge market hedge side with all kinds of weird mysteries going on in a reliable location, mages would be on that like flies on shit and there is no way Changeling's could keep that a secret from Mages, not at Kensington Market or at such size, especially when the Changeligs don't run the Goblin Markets.<br /> <br /> And the CN Tower, have a CN Tower hedge side is bound to cause all kinds of weird stuff to go on, again drawing Mages too it.<br /> <br /> Heck given Mages addiction to Mysteries, I can see Changeling delibrately using Fae secrets, the ones that are no threat to Changelings, like a drug dealer in reguards to Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T18:08:27-07:00","id":851491,"title":"","content":"The problem with the Hedge is that for Mages it's easier to get in than out. Not that that's stopping anybody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T08:46:59-07:00","id":851788,"title":"","content":"There are likely relatively safe locations for Mages in the Hedge like the Kensington Goblin Market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T08:49:17-07:00","id":851792,"title":"","content":"Safe doesn't mean you can get out easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:17:01-07:00","id":852714,"title":"","content":"Going with the diversity of the city perhaps instead of being dominated by the Pentacle Toronto could be home to several ancient Nameless Orders from around the world. Tao Sorcerers, Houdon Priests, Shamans, Druids, whatever fits with the background of each neighborhood. The Pentacle would of course still be present, but as one of numerous orders all struggling for new members and to maintain traditions.<br /> \u200bAlso, if Packs can now contain non Werewolf members, what about Cabals and Mages? How about Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:24:23-07:00","id":852717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=852714#post852714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going with the diversity of the city perhaps instead of being dominated by the Pentacle Toronto could be home to several ancient Nameless Orders from around the world. Tao Sorcerers, Houdon Priests, Shamans, Druids, whatever fits with the background of each neighborhood. The Pentacle would of course still be present, but as one of numerous orders all struggling for new members and to maintain traditions.<br /> \u200bAlso, if Packs can now contain non Werewolf members, what about Cabals and Mages? How about Changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe if those mortal occult practices hadn't been absorbed into the Orders already a long time ago. I think when making a Nameless Order it's better to find a broad archetype that isn't found in the other Orders rather than really small niches that are, or at least a very divergent philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-24-2016, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:24:45-07:00","id":852718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=852714#post852714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAlso, if Packs can now contain non Werewolf members, what about Cabals and Mages? How about Changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that your question could be answered by the fact that the Appendix on mortals in Mage 2e is entitled <b>Punching Up</b>. (Read: Yes, non-Mage can be part of Cabals)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:28:07-07:00","id":852720,"title":"","content":"The Pentacle Orders may have absorbed them but that doesn't mean everyone jumped on the bus. Besides there will be some groups they didn't absorb, otherwise where do Nameless Orders come from post the Great Refusal? The idea is to have Nameless Orders that fit the different cultures, the examples given where just the first things that came to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:29:50-07:00","id":852721,"title":"","content":"It's not that I disagree with you as much as it is that when someone starts throwing around the Nameless Order idea I prefer a take that actually rocks the boat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:51:36-07:00","id":852734,"title":"","content":"The thought was that in Toronto maybe the local Mages are tied more into their respective cultures than that of the Pentacle, be it Atlantian or the hodgepodge of the Free Council. Chinese Mages are representative of Chinese culture and views on magic and so on, instead of all being united by a common Mage subculture.<br /> \u200bIt would be taking the ghetto or boroughs and extending them to include the magical world, with all of the divisiveness and ethnocentrism that implies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 03-24-2016, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T19:14:32-07:00","id":852749,"title":"","content":"The Pentacle isn't Eurocentric; it's a global conspiracy. There's no reason to assume that Mages from China or Jamaica or Haiti or Russia or India or wherever are Nameless by default.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Mysterium term for political clout is Chinese. It is that way for a reason.<br /> <br /> That said, Orders aren't identical across the world. Until they get down to talking brass tacks, the Pentacle doesn't look identical in Ireland and Mexico; China and Australia; Peru and Iran.<br /> <br /> Everywhere has local flavours, heresies, practiced, languages, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T19:42:11-07:00","id":852759,"title":"","content":"Yeah, with an understanding that I'm not trying to shit on the idea, I think just going with Nameless Orders that mimic ethnic mystical practices would be a very surface read of the diversity of Toronto, and my own issue is the caveat that I actually do want the Consilium to be archetypal in its structure, even if it has something to complicate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T21:48:05-07:00","id":852795,"title":"","content":"If that's the case then my suggestion isn't what you are after, but to clarify what I was aiming at was a city where the Mages aren't part of a global conspiracy, where they where concerned only with their own and as far as the Chinese (or any other group) was concerned the Irish better stay on their side of the street. My intent was a city where the Mages not only didn't cooperate or share a common core, but one where they didn't want anything to do with each other, where the rule of the day is 'stick to your own'.<br /> \u200bIf what you want is the standard Consillium but with a complication then give them something they don't agree on, a mystery that the Arrow see as a threat, the Guardians think should be quarantined, the Mysterium want to study and the Council intend to share, all while the Ladder thinks it rightfully belongs to them. Make it something that CLEARLY isn't Atlantian nor obviously of the Abyss, something of obvious value that may just up end the whole Atlantis story.<br /> \u200bAnother alternative, a city where the Seers are dominant and they have found a way to almost completely stifle awakenings. It's a city where nothing major seems to happen because the powers that be stomp down anything potentially disruptive before it can happen. Treat the Consillium like an underground criminal organization fighting against a tyrannical government, taking every new Awakened as a vital gift, while they desperately search for the secret of how the Seers did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 03-25-2016, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T08:54:51-07:00","id":852994,"title":"","content":"I actually like the idea of awhole bunch of nameless orders, not just based on cultures, but interests,subcultures, ect...<br /> <br /> But I see the Nameless Orders as a buffer zone between the Seers of the Throne and the Pentacle who are in a cold war, trying to influence the nameless orders and their members as proxies are how the two major groups compete for resources, new members (absorbeding a nameless order or making an alliance with an order).<br /> <br /> I'm thinking a kind of USA vs USSR vibe, with new mages, nameless orders and other groups like mystery cults acting as proxy states, and targets for conquest in some cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:41:17-07:00","id":853087,"title":"","content":"An Order isn't just a hobby or a political alliance; it (usually) reflects a profound belief in the nature of the cosmos and one's purpose within it. Nameless Orders exist for those who either do not have sufficient cultural contact with the Pentacle or Seers, or whose traditions diverge from them strongly. If you have a strong interest or cultural affiliation, that's the basis for a cabal or a faction, but it'd have to be all-consuming to be the basis of something as grand as an Order.<br /> <br /> Also, none of that really fits Toronto's vibe. There is no Cold War divide between cultures. The city embraces diversity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T22:10:32-07:00","id":853337,"title":"","content":"Then for a real twist make it the city where the Pentacle really works, that alone would be a mystery for the ages and one every Ladder would love to solve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T00:35:54-07:00","id":853375,"title":"","content":"A city where the Pentacle really works is one that doesn't have much in the way of conflict, since it ostensibly has a functioning government and reasonable, far-sighted populace.<br /> <br /> It's like suggesting setting your political thriller in a world where Congress is incorruptible and educated: Sure, it'd be nice, but where's the drama and conflict?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:43:48-07:00","id":853504,"title":"","content":"I imagine that like The Culture, the drama and conflict would come from the Consilieum's interaction with outsiders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T09:48:23-07:00","id":853543,"title":"","content":"How about this, the Consillium works because they are all busy struggling against a common threat, the reason the city seems so quiet is because every member of the Pentacle fights to keep it that way. Think something similar to a Vampire court under open siege by the Strix. I'm not saying this is the chronicle I would run, it's just an idea that might fit the situation described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T12:56:01-07:00","id":853632,"title":"","content":"Right, but why? The Consilium isn't the interesting part, there; it's the threat.<br /> <br /> Conflict is the source of drama, not flawlessness. And if the conflict is purely external, you give up all the lovely complications of doubt, paranoia, zeal, disagreement, etc.<br /> <br /> What do you really get in exchange for giving that up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T13:06:10-07:00","id":853640,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I'm not saying I'm looking for a highly functional, flawless Consilium, but rather an archetypal one. As in, there's an alliance between the Council of Free Assemblies and the Diamond, there's a Hierarch, Mages haven't broken off ties in favor of lawlessness or paranoia (yet), etcetera. <br /> <br /> That doesn't remotely mean a conflict-free Consilium, just one that looks like one would expect one to look like based on the books.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm getting some ideas for conflict.<ul><li>Tensions between the Pentacle Mages and the Apostates who live in the city. Presumably they are also attracted by the same Mystery that whets the appetites of Pentacle Mages, but for their own reasons. Thematically it does tie into the diversity proposed for Toronto, while also engaging in the tensions that arise from having people from very different places/perspectives living side by side. There's also probably conflict between the Diamond and the Council on what to do with Apostates that cause trouble and the like.</li> <li> The Chalice Compact. I'm thinking less that the Tremere secretly run the Consilium and more that they have a few plants in the various Caucuses. Should it be a secret that the Chalice Compact even exists, or should it be one of those things that's a rumor, a strawman you use against people you don't like and a well-founded fear?</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Do those sound like good ways to complicate the Consilium? Do you guys have any additional suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T16:54:19-07:00","id":853746,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm not a huge fan of the Chalice Compact. If you're already willing to give the Tremere a source of blackmail and a gun to your head, and you're apparently okay with them preying on people, why not skip a step and just join them already?<br /> <br /> It feels more like a thing that the Tremere do to people than as something they'd offer by way of service.<br /> <br /> Also, there's an assumption that the Apostates are more diverse than the Diamond. Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T17:19:45-07:00","id":853754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=853746#post853746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm not a huge fan of the Chalice Compact. If you're already willing to give the Tremere a source of blackmail and a gun to your head, and you're apparently okay with them preying on people, why not skip a step and just join them already?<br /> <br /> It feels more like a thing that the Tremere do to people than as something they'd offer by way of service.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. I'm not married to it, just thinking something could be done to utilize it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=853746#post853746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there's an assumption that the Apostates are more diverse than the Diamond. Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>The diversity I was discussing was in terms of viewpoint and ideology. There is diversity within the Diamond and the Council, of course, but I was thinking of the diversity in terms of the many reasons why they wouldn't want to be Diamond. Council or Seers. Like, they're used to diversity of thought <i>within </i>the Pentacle, but those who abstain from membership might have ideological differences even more significant than that between a Mysterium member and a Free Councillor.<br /> <br /> To a lesser extent, I think it also reflects Apostates from around the world. There might be one from London, another from Taipei, another from South Carolina, et al. <br /> <br /> I imagine Apostates are very singular types of people, and consequently, you're not gonna find too many in one place, unless they're coming from other places and concentrating in that place. I imagine that place to be Toronto.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T17:44:07-07:00","id":853766,"title":"","content":"So you need a mystery which draws people from all over, somewhat singular, and also a reason that certain key individuals might tolerate a cell of Tremere.<br /> <br /> You're looking for a mystery about souls that draws Reapers - Reapers that the Tremere hunt and that the establishment always suspects apostates of secretly being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T19:38:27-07:00","id":853821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=853632#post853632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but why? The Consilium isn't the interesting part, there; it's the threat.<br /> <br /> Conflict is the source of drama, not flawlessness. And if the conflict is purely external, you give up all the lovely complications of doubt, paranoia, zeal, disagreement, etc.<br /> <br /> What do you really get in exchange for giving that up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it would be more fun to use a surface layer of being more cooperative than usual only to find out that the dysfunctions are buried deeper down, come up with and explore the reasons why etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=853746#post853746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm not a huge fan of the Chalice Compact. If you're already willing to give the Tremere a source of blackmail and a gun to your head, and you're apparently okay with them preying on people, why not skip a step and just join them already?<br /> <br /> It feels more like a thing that the Tremere do to people than as something they'd offer by way of service.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having someone in office who isn't a Tremere removes a level of risk for the Tremere operating in Toronto. They can have a candidate for Heirarch who appears legitimate to the magical scrutiny of the Consilium, but will ultimately follow their plans because they really don't have a choice unless they resort to soul stealing themselves. (Sidenote: I wonder what happens if you try to place a soul into yourself after you are under the effects of the Chalice. Technically, there's a void there, but metaphysically, you're whole.)<br /> <br /> It is a definitely a gun to your head. They boost you to Heirarch if you forfeit your soul, and you can't become Heirarch without their support. There really wasn't any talk in Left Hand Path about just how many Heirarchs they've gone through, and there definitely wasn't any mention of them giving souls back. I would not at all be surprised to find it a common practice for them to choose the next person they offer the position too. This could in fact be why the Orders might appear to work together so well in Toronto on the surface. They groom exceptional diplomats and politicians to take the job, but underneath they pressure the Heirarch to sabotage the Orders that the Heirarch doesn't belong too. People find out about the subsurface corruption and favoritism of the Heirarch for his Order and boot him, the Tremere devour their soul for failing them and give their next puppet the leg up keeping the involvement of the Tremere on another, lower layer of subterfuge and sabotage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=853754#post853754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine Apostates are very singular types of people, and consequently, you're not gonna find too many in one place, unless they're coming from other places and concentrating in that place. I imagine that place to be Toronto.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe instead of Apostates you could toy with Solitares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=853766#post853766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're looking for a mystery about souls that draws Reapers - Reapers that the Tremere hunt and that the establishment always suspects apostates of secretly being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm imagining a weird intersection between the Tremere and the cult of the World Dragon where the Tremere in Toronto have latched onto the idea that Hallows which can be used by the cult of the World Dragon show evidence that the world has a soul that can be accessed outside of the Astral. If they could manage to create a House of the World Dragon by successfully devouring the soul of a cult member and incorporating their attainments it might give the Tremere the ability to devour chunks of the soul of the world itself in their quest for the Final Tower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-26-2016, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T22:26:32-07:00","id":860128,"title":"","content":"So I was mulling it over randomly today, and I had one possible idea for a big Mystery that multiple groups might be interested in.<br /> <br /> What if, in Toronto, there are certain places where, if the proper pattern of behavior or activity is observed, cracks open in reality, that allow instantaneous transportation to random places? It could be another part of Toronto, or it could be another city in the world, like Baghdad, or it could be another realm, like the Shadow, or even weirder places, like Atlantean ruins. The problem is, these places where you can attempt to open these cracks in reality seem to appear in totally random places for limited time frames, and few Mages seem to understand how to make it open up to the place you want to go.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem is that it's a two-way street. You open up a crack to the Underworld, you can go there, but whatever is on the other side can come through, too. If it opens to Dubai, you can go there, but whoever is in Dubai can go back too. Mages from around the world might be interested in figuring out how to make it work both in Toronto and where these cracks open up, and groups like the Seers and the Pentacle might be very interested in controlling a means of effortlessly accessing anywhere from different cities to different timelines.<br /> <br /> They might conceptualize it as a device, though I'm thinking that it's part of the metaphor (or possibly a crazy theory) that it is a device that does this.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think of that?<br /> <br /> My inspiration is that I think portals to anywhere are cool, a versatile storytelling device, a means of accessing a lot of different and interesting locations, <i>and </i>the Legacy called the Reality Stalkers, who might see Toronto as the place where their legacy's philosophy and actual capability is expressed most powerfully. Might give me an excuse to update them to the 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> I'm totally open to feedback that might tighten or focus this concept, too, if anyone thinks there are ways to improve it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-06-2016, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T23:08:58-07:00","id":860141,"title":"","content":"I was going to suggest that you use the Tremere but without the Chalice. After all a centuries old Mage is going to have plenty to bribe, threaten and blackmail with without relying on a magic cup (even if it never spills). They also have several puppets within the Consillium and even Seers, but none of the puppets know who else is wearing strings so they don't know who they can trust.<br /> \u200bAs for the cracks in reality, I would have one of the cracks that sometimes appears lead to somewhere the Mages don't know and can't find again no matter what Space combination they use, one that always expels them when the crack closes. Then give it a desirable trait, like a lack of Paradox, that draws both Pentacle, Seers and the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T03:04:30-07:00","id":860202,"title":"","content":"So refining the concept, I'm thinking Mages call them Rifts, and that they sometimes reach places that Mages could not reach even with their Arcana, while also reaching more mundane places. I'm also thinking that a few attentive Mages have noticed that more Rifts appear the more immigrants Toronto has. What this means or how it interacts with the Rifts is still a mystery,<br /> <br /> I'm also thinking that most Rifts are unstable. They appear, temporarily, then disappear, with a very small number of &quot;stable&quot; rifts that some Mages or other factions take advantage of and control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T00:30:28-07:00","id":860844,"title":"","content":"Just curious but how will these Rifts interact with Sleepers and other supernatural splats? Also, you spelled Rifts with a capital 'R', are we harkening back to the old RPG?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T01:40:42-07:00","id":860863,"title":"","content":"No, I was just trying to call it Rifts with a capital R to indicate they're a proper thing distinct from any other old portal.<br /> <br /> I have thought about it. I think one of the stable Rifts lead into the shadow and the Old Lake Dominion, the Werewolf protectorate in the area, may have sealed it while assuming it was the product of something they knew about. They haven't encountered any other Rifts.<br /> <br /> the Kindred of Toronto are too busy being Kindred to notice or care about the Rifts.<br /> <br /> The Demons of Toronto are aware of them and use them. Unfortunately, so does the Machine.<br /> <br /> It takes a particular kind of occult knowledge/the capabilities of Arcana to interact with the Rifts, so it kind of makes sense that Demons, Mages and the Machine wind up being the ones that use them. I suspect most Mages don't encounter the Rifts that the Machine is already using, because they're hidden away by Infrastructure and Facilities. Demons that use them seriously are pretty rare, because suddenly winding up in Capetown is usually a pretty serious breach of Cover.<br /> <br /> There might be some mortals who can sense the Rifts, and an even rarer few who can just activate them with a minor expenditure of effort. All of them are the children of immigrants that arrived within the city after the dawn of the 21st century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T21:37:02-07:00","id":861581,"title":"","content":"Do the Demons, Mages and Machine see these gifted mortals as valuable resources, like Stigmatics or Proximi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T21:26:17-07:00","id":863000,"title":"","content":"After talking it over with a friend, we contemplated the idea of calling them Tears instead of Rifts, which feels like it could lend itself to a cool tapestry/fabric metaphor and fits them a bit better since they're sort of like tears in the fabric of space and time. They also appear more frequently when the city's population is in flux, either increasing in number or decreasing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850434-a-mage-toronto-setting?p=861581#post861581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Demons, Mages and Machine see these gifted mortals as valuable resources, like Stigmatics or Proximi?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not seen like Proximi per se, but I think Stigmatics are a fair comparison. The Awakened might have to resist the temptation to treat them like tools, since they really are just tools for opening the Tears.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that there could be a cabal of Banishers who seek those people out and kill them in addition to Mages they discover to be making headway on the Tears. Something to mull over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T15:45:57-07:00","id":863943,"title":"","content":"If you include such Banishers might I recommend that you create a long lasting cabal that traces its origins to some terrible event (or near event) involving the Tears in the past. Not only will that lend to making them more interesting as a group but they might have their own records of the Tears for Mages to steal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T18:04:38-07:00","id":866588,"title":"","content":"So my girlfriend and I were talking about the Seers today, thinking about Tetrarchs that could feasibly operate in the area. While we could describe multiple ones, I think one big one could suffice, but we're otherwise wondering what the Seers should look like in Toronto and the level of influence they should have. <br /> <br /> As an aside, should it ever come up, we've decided to take Idola from Imperial Mysteries, and broaden her influence to include Eastern Canada, though going with her original description most of her focus/attention goes to the East Coast of the United States.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any thoughts on what Ministries might be big here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T19:21:37-07:00","id":866609,"title":"","content":"In Toronto which is big on diversity? I could see the Unity being a big deal. Ostensibly trying to unite the different cultures into an accepting and welcoming environment for people from all over the world and secretly grinding their individuality into dust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T18:51:20-07:00","id":1073490,"title":"","content":"I live in Toronto and reading this thread, I'd have the city caught in a brutal war between Unity and Mammon Ministers, one so bad that the Pentacle just tries to keep out of the way of, but never get involved in. <br /> <br /> I suggested adding Mammon because Toronto is the fincial capital of Canada. Bay Street in Toronto is Canada's Wall Street, with the TSX being the third largest stock exchange in North America, and Toronto has a massive impact on mining, if your in the mining business odds are been in Toronto (mining is important to Toronto, but it doesn't occur in Toronto). <br /> <br /> Many of the most famous PUAs (seductionists) come from Toronto, the most famous being Mystery, who get this is also a serious Magician. <br /> <br /> Famous locations, CN Tower, Kensington Market, Skydome, Ripply's Believe it or not Aquruim, the Toronto Zoo, the Science Centre, there is a underground convention centre I forget what it's called, that is the size of 10 foot ball fields, maple leaf gardens, the Rogers Centre, Thousand Islands. <br /> <br /> The most famous strip club is the Brass Rail, it was the location of the strip club in the American Pie: Beta House movie, but if you want any action to go to the Trinity Clubs in Missuaga, Cafe Altantis, Loco, and the Midway Invader. I tend to visit Whiskey Agogo and Vaughan Spa beside it in Vaughan, just above the City of Toronto. <br /> <br /> The GTA (Greater Toronto area, not grand theft auto, common mistake) is made up of the City of Toronto, York Region, Peel Region, Halton Region, and Durham Region. Seriously the Metropolitan region of Toronto is huge, will millions of people. <br /> <br /> Given the diversity talk there are two cities within the GTA that actual have Caucians as a minority, Markham, largest group Chinese and Brampton which has East Indians being the largest population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}